hadiths[283]{hadithnumber,text}:
"705.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Asma bint Umays that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"
"705.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from Asma bint Umays that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah"
"706.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu'l-Hulayfa and Abu Bakr told her to do ghusl and then enter ihram"
"706.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu'l-Hulayfa and Abu Bakr told her to do ghusl and then enter ihram"
"707.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn Umar used to do ghusl for ihram before he entered ihram"
"707.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi' that 'Abdullah ibn Umar used to do ghusl for ihram before he entered ihram"
"708.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from his father Abdullah ibn Hunayn that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama once had a disagreement at al-Abwa. Abdullah said that some one in ihram could wash his head"
"708.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn from his father Abdullah ibn Hunayn that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama once had a disagreement at al-Abwa. Abdullah said that some one in ihram could wash his head"
"709.1","Malik related to me from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that 'Umar ibn alKhattab once asked Yala ibn Munya"
"709.2","Malik related to me from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that 'Umar ibn alKhattab once asked Yala ibn Munya"
"710.1","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would spend the night between the two trails in the valley of Dhu Tuwa when he was approaching Makka. Then he would pray subh"
"710.2","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would spend the night between the two trails in the valley of Dhu Tuwa when he was approaching Makka. Then he would pray subh"
"711.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would never wash his head while he was in ihram except if he had to do ghusl because of a wet dream. Malik said"
"711.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar would never wash his head while he was in ihram except if he had to do ghusl because of a wet dream. Malik said"
"712.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man once asked the Messenger of Allah"
"712.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man once asked the Messenger of Allah"
"713.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"713.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"714.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he had heard Aslam"
"714.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he had heard Aslam"
"715.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Asma bint Abi Bakr had worn clothes that were completely dyed with safflower while she was in ihram"
"715.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Asma bint Abi Bakr had worn clothes that were completely dyed with safflower while she was in ihram"
"716.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to disapprove of anybody wearing a belt or girdle while in ihram"
"716.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to disapprove of anybody wearing a belt or girdle while in ihram"
"717.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab say"
"717.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id that he heard Said ibn al Musayyab say"
"718.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that al-Furafisa ibn Umayr al-Hanafi saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj"
"718.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said that al-Furafisa ibn Umayr al-Hanafi saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj"
"719.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that he was asked about a man in i'tikaf: does he enter under a roof for his need? He said: Yes, there is no harm in that. Malik said: The matter with us, concerning which there is no disagreement, is that i'tikaf is not disliked in any mosque where Jumu'ah is held. And I do not see it disliked in mosques where Jumu'ah is not held, except due to the dislike that the person in i'tikaf might leave his mosque for Jumu'ah or abandon it. If it is a mosque where Jumu'ah is not held and its owner is not obliged to attend Jumu'ah in another mosque, then I see no harm in i'tikaf therein, because Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: {And you are in i'tikaf in the mosques} (2:187). So Allah generalized all mosques and did not specify any of them. Malik said: From this it is permitted for him to do i'tikaf in mosques where Jumu'ah is not held, provided he is not obliged to leave it for the mosque where Jumu'ah is held. Malik said: The person in i'tikaf does not sleep except in the mosque where he is doing i'tikaf, unless his tent is in a courtyard of the mosque. I have not heard that the person in i'tikaf erects a building to sleep in except in the mosque or in a courtyard of the mosque. And what indicates that he does not sleep except in the mosque is the statement of Aisha: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he did i'tikaf, would not enter the house except for a human need."" And he does not do i'tikaf on the roof of the mosque nor in the minaret, meaning the sawma'ah (hermitage). Malik said: The person in i'tikaf enters the place where he intends to do i'tikaf before the sunset of the night in which he intends to begin i'tikaf, so that he receives the first night of his i'tikaf with his i'tikaf. The person in i'tikaf is occupied with his i'tikaf; he does not engage in anything else of what he might occupy himself with, such as trade or otherwise. There is no harm in his ordering some of his needs regarding his property and the welfare of his family, and ordering the sale of his property or something that does not occupy him personally. There is no harm in that if it is light, that he orders someone who suffices him in it. Malik said: I have not heard anyone from the people of knowledge mention a condition for i'tikaf. Rather, i'tikaf is an act among acts, like prayer, fasting, and Hajj, and similar acts. Whatever of that was an obligation or a supererogatory act, whoever enters into something of that acts only according to the Sunnah that has passed. It is not for him to innovate in that anything other than what the Muslims have passed upon, neither a condition he stipulates nor an innovation he introduces. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did i'tikaf, and the Muslims knew the Sunnah of i'tikaf. Malik said: I'tikaf and jiwar (neighboring/staying in the mosque) are the same. And i'tikaf for the city-dweller and the bedouin are the same."
"719.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a man in ihram should not veil anything above his chin"
"720.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar shrouded his son Waqid ibn Abdullah"
"720.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar shrouded his son Waqid ibn Abdullah"
"721.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a woman in ihram should wear neither a veil nor gloves"
"721.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say that a woman in ihram should wear neither a veil nor gloves"
"722.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Fatima bint al-Mundhir said"
"722.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Fatima bint al-Mundhir said"
"723.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"723.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"724.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Rabah that a bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah"
"724.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays from Ata ibn Rabah that a bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah"
"725.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Aslam"
"725.2","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger
of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to go to
relieve himself in houses.


Malik said, ""Someone doing itikaf
should not leave for his parents' funeral or for anything else."""
"726.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from as-Salt ibn Zubayd from more than one of his family that Umar ibn al-Khattab discovered the smell of perfume while he was at ash-Shajara. Kathir ibn as-Salt was at his side"
"726.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from as-Salt ibn Zubayd from more than one of his family that Umar ibn al-Khattab discovered the smell of perfume while he was at ash-Shajara. Kathir ibn as-Salt was at his side"
"727.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Walid ibn Abd al- Malik asked Salim ibn Abdullah and Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit if he could use perfume after he had stoned the jamra and shaved his head"
"727.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that al-Walid ibn Abd al- Malik asked Salim ibn Abdullah and Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit if he could use perfume after he had stoned the jamra and shaved his head"
"728.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"728.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"729.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"729.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"730.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at al-Fur"
"730.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at al-Fur"
"731.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at Ilya (Jerusalem)"
"731.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from a reliable source that Abdullah ibn Umar once entered ihram at Ilya (Jerusalem)"
"732.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"732.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"733.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Umar that the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah"
"733.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Umar that the talbiya of the Messenger of Allah"
"734.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"734.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"735","Yahya related to me from Malik from Musa ibn Uqba that Salim ibn Abdullah heard his father say"
"736","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi that Ubayd ibn Jurayj once said to Abdullah ibn Umar"
"737","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to pray in the mosque of Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"738","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abd al- Malik ibn Marwan had started to do talbiya at the mosque of Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"739","Yahya related to me from Malik from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Khallad ibn as-Sa'ib al-Ansari from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"740","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say"
"741","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, who was an orphan under the guardianship of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Hajj al-Ifrad."
"742","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abu'l-Aswad Muhammad ibn 'Abd ar-Rahman, from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr, from A'isha, umm al-muminin, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, did hajj on its own"
"743","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say"
"744","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, that he asked Anas ibn Malik - while they were going from Mina to Arafah - \How did you used to do on this day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""The one who was making talbiyah would make talbiyah and would not be forbidden from it"
"745","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard some of the people of knowledge say"
"746","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she used to abandon talbiyah when she returned to the standing place (al-Mawqif)."
"747","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to stop talbiyah during Hajj when he reached the Haram, until he performed Tawaf around the House and between Safa and Marwah, then he would make talbiyah, until he went from Mina to Arafah. When he went, he would abandon talbiyah, and he used to abandon talbiyah during Umrah when he entered the Haram."
"748","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that he used to say: Abdullah ibn Umar did not perform the talbiyah while performing tawaf around the House."
"749","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab used to say, ""Abdullah ibn Umar would never say the talbiya while he was doing tawaf of the House"
"750","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz went out on the Day of Arafah from Mina, and he heard the takbir loudly. He sent the guards to shout to the people: \O people"
"751","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \O people of Makkah"
"752","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr stayed in Makkah for nine years, performing ihlal for Hajj upon seeing the crescent of Dhu al-Hijjah, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr was with him doing that."
"753","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwa, that Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr stayed in Makka for nine years. He would go into ihram for hajj at the beginning of Dhu'l-Hijja, and Urwa ibn az- Zubayr, who was with him, would do likewise. Yahya said that Malik said, ""The people of Makka and whoever else is living there besides them should go into ihram for hajj if they are in Makka, and anyone that is living in the centre of Makka and is not one of the people of Makka should not leave the Haram."" Yahya said that Malik said, ""Someone who goes into ihram for hajj in Makka should delay tawaf of the House and the sa'y between Safa and Marwa until he has come back from Mina, which is what Abdullah ibn Umar used to do."" Malik was asked what the people of Madina, or anybody else, should do about tawaf if they went into ihram in Makka at the beginning of Dhu'l-Hijja, and he said, ""They should delay the obligatory tawaf, which is the one they combine with the say between Safa and Marwa, but they can do whatever other tawaf they want to, and they should pray two rakas every time they complete seven tawafs, which is what the companions of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, did when they had gone into ihram to do hajj. They delayed the tawaf of the House and the sa'y between Safa and Marwa until they had come back from Mina. Abdullah ibn Umar also did this, going into ihram for hajj in Makka at the beginning of Dhu'l-Hijja, and then delaying tawaf of theHouse and the say between Safa and Marwa until he had come back from Mina."" Malik was asked whether one of the people of Makka could go into ihram to do umra in the centre of Makka, and he said, ""No. He should go outside the Haram and go into ihram there"
"754","Yahya bin Sa'id informed me, from Malik, that he asked 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman about one who sends his sacrificial animal and stays, whether anything becomes forbidden to him. She informed him that she heard 'A'ishah say: \Nothing becomes forbidden except for one who enters the state of Ihram and says the Talbiyah.\"""""
"755","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"756","Yahya informed me, from Malik, from Nafi', that 'Abd Allah bin 'Umar used to say: \A menstruating woman who enters the state of Ihram for Hajj or 'Umrah"
"757","Yahya informed me, from Malik, that it reached him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'Umrah three times: in the year of Hudaybiyyah, in the year of Qada', and in the year of Ji'ranah."
"758","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"759","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa"
"760","Yahya informed me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id bin al-Musayyab, that 'Umar bin Abi Salamah sought permission from 'Umar bin al-Khattab to perform 'Umrah in Shawwal. He gave him permission, so he performed 'Umrah, then he returned to his family and did not perform Hajj."
"761","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he would cease the talbiyah for Umrah when he entered the Haram."
"762","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn 'Urwa, that his father would stop saying the talbiya when he entered the Haram, if he was doing 'umra. Malik said that someone who went into ihram at at-Tanim should stop saying the talbiya when he saw the House. Yahya said that Malik was asked where a man from the people of Madina, or elsewhere, who had begun doing umra at one of the mawaqit, should stop saying the talbiya, and he said, ""Someone who goes into ihram at one of the mawaqit should stop saying the talbiya when he arrives at the Haram."" Malik added, ""I have heard that Abdullah ibn Umar used to do that"
"763","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he said: \By Allah"
"764","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he used to say: \Whoever performs Umrah in the months of Hajj"
"765","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that he heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab saying: \Whoever performs Umrah in Shawwal"
"766","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said used to hear Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"767","Malik said, ""Someone who does umra in Shawwal, Dhu'l-Qada or Dhu'l-Hijja and then goes back to his people, and then returns and does hajj in that same year does not have to sacrifice an animal. Sacrificing an animal is only incumbent on some one who does umra in the months of hajj, and then stays in Makka and then does hajj. A person not from Makka who moves to Makka and establishes his home there and does umra in the months of the hajj and then begins his hajj there is not doing tamattu. He does not have to sacrifice an animal nor does he have to fast. He is in the same position as the people of Makka if he is one of those who are living there."" Malik was asked whether a man from Makka who had gone to live in another town or had been on a journey and then returned to Makka with the intention of staying there, regardless of whether he had a family there or not, and entered it to do umra in the months of the hajj, and then began his hajj there, beginning his umra at the miqat of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, or at a place nearer than that, was doing tamattu or not? Malik answered, ""He does not have to sacrifice an animal or fast as someone who is doing tamattu has to do. This is because Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says in His Book, 'That is for someone whose family are not present at Masjid al-Haram. ' Yahya related to me from Malik, from Sumayy, the mawla of Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman, from Abu Salih as-Samman, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace ,said, ""Umra is an expiation for what is between it and the next umra, and the only reward for an accepted hajj is the Garden"
"768","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: \Separate your Hajj and your Umrah"
"769","Yahya related to me from Malik that it reached him that Uthman ibn Affan, when he performed Umrah, would sometimes not dismount from his riding-beast until he returned."
"770","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Uthman ibn Affan would sometimes never get down from the animal he was riding on when he was doing umra"
"771","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, brother of the Banu Abd al-Dar, that Umar ibn Ubaydullah sent to Aban ibn Uthman, and Aban was the Amir al-Hajj at that time, while they were both in the state of Ihram. He said: \I intend to marry Talhah ibn Umar to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr"
"772","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, that Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri informed him that his father Tarif had married a woman while he was in the state of Ihram, and Umar ibn al-Khattab annulled his marriage."
"773","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say: The one in the state of Ihram shall not marry, nor propose for himself, nor for anyone else."
"774","Yahya related to me from Malik that it reached him that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, Salim ibn Abdullah, and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked about the marriage of one in the state of Ihram. They said: The one in the state of Ihram shall not marry, nor give in marriage."
"775","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab"
"776","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he used to say: The one in the state of Ihram shall not have cupping done except out of necessity."
"777","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say, ""Someone in ihram should not be cupped, except when there is no other alternative."" Malik said, ""Someone who is in ihram should not be cupped except when it is necessary"
"778","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Zubayr ibn al-Awwam used to take dried meat of gazelles as provisions while he was in the state of Ihram."
"779","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Ata ibn Yasar informed him, from Abu Qatadah, concerning the wild ass, similar to the narration of Abu al-Nadr, except that in the narration of Zayd ibn Aslam, it is stated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do you have any of its meat?\"""""
"780","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Ata ibn Yasar had told him, from Abu Qatada, the same hadith about the wild ass as that of Abu'n-Nadr, except that in the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Do you still have any of its meat?"
"781","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari said that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi told him from Isa ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah"
"782","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab relating from Abu Hurayra that he was once coming back from Bahrayn, and, when he reached ar-Rabadha, he found a caravan of people from Iraq in ihram, who asked him whether they could eat the meat of some game which they had found with the people of ar- Rabadha, and he told them they could eat it. He said, ""Afterwards I had doubts about what I had told them to do, so when I got back to Madina I mentioned the matter to Umar ibn al-Khattab and he said, 'What did you tell them to do?' I said, ' I told them to eat it.' Umar ibn al-Khattab said, threatening me, 'If you had told them to do anything else I would have done something to you"
"783","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that Salim ibn Abdullah heard Abu Hurayra relating to Abdullah ibn Umar how a group of three people in ihram had passed him at ar-Rabadha and had asked him for a fatwa about eating game which people who were not in ihram were eating, and he told them that they could eat it. He said, ""Then I went to Umar ibn al-Khattab in Madina and asked him about it, and he said, 'What did you say to them?' and I said, 'I told them that they could eat it.' Umar said, 'If you had told them anything else I would have done you an injury"
"784","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Sa'b ibn Jaththamah al-Laythi, that he presented a wild ass as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abwa' or Wuddan. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the expression on his face, he said: \We did not return it to you except that we are in a state of Ihram.\"""""
"785","I was narrated to, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rab'ah, who said: \I saw Uthman ibn Affan at al-Arj"
"786","I was narrated to, from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, that she said to him: \O son of my sister"
"787","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There are five kinds of vermin that a pilgrim in the state of Ihram is not guilty of killing: the crow"
"788","Malik said, ""It is not halal to eat any game that has been hunted in the Haram, or has had a dog set after it in the Haram and then been killed outside the Haram. Anyone that does that has to pay a forfeit for what has been hunted. However, some one that sets his dog after game outside the Haram and then follows it until it is hunted down in the Haram does not have to pay any forfeit, unless he set the dog after the game near to the Haram. The game should not be eaten, however. If he set the dog loose near the Haram then he has to pay a forfeit for the game."" Malik said, ""Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says, 'O you who trust, do not kill game while you are in ihram. Whoever of you kills game intentionally has to pay a forfeit commensurate with what he has killed in cattle which two men from among you shall judge, a sacrificial animal which reaches the Kaba, or else he makes a kaffara of either feeding poor people or the equivalent of that in fasting, so that he may taste the consequences of what he has done.' "" (Sura 5 ayat 95). Malik said, ""Someone who hunts game when he is not in ihram and then kills it while he is in ihram is in the same position as someone who buys game while he is in ihram and then kills it. Allah has forbidden killing it, and so a man who does so has to pay a forfeit for it. The position that we go by in this matter is that a forfeit is assessed for anyone who kills game while he is in ihram."" Yahya said that Malik said, ""The best that I have heard about someone who kills game and is assessed for it is that the game which he has killed is assessed and its value in food is estimated and with that food he feeds each poor man a mudd, or fasts a day in place of each mudd. The number of poor men is considered, and if it is ten then he fasts ten days, and if it is twenty he fasts twenty days, according to how many people there are to be fed, even if there are more than sixty."" Malik said, ""I have heard that a forfeit is assessed for someone who kills game in the Haram while he is not in ihram in the same way that it is assessed for some one who kills game in the Haram while he is in ihram ."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""There are five kinds of animal which it is not wrong for some one in ihram to kill:crows, kites, scorpions, rats and mice, and wild dogs"
"789","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"790","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"791","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umar ibn al- Khattab told people to kill snakes in the Haram. Malik said"
"792","Yahya related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn alHarith at-Taymi from Rabia ibn Abi Abdullah ibn alHudayr that he saw Umar ibn al-Khattab taking the ticks off a camel of his at as- Suqya while he was in ihram . Malik said that he disapproved of that"
"793","Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said"
"794","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Musa that Abdullah ibn Umar once looked in the mirror for something that was irritating him while he was in ihram"
"795","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar did not like people who were in ihram removing mites or ticks from their camels. Malik said"
"796","Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam once asked Said ibn al-Musayyab about (what to do with) a nail of his that had broken while he was in ihram and Said said"
"797","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas said"
"798","Yahya related to me that Malik said, ""Someone whose passage to the House is blocked by an enemy is freed from every restriction of ihram, and should sacrifice his animal and shave his head wherever he has been detained, and there is nothing for him to make up afterwards."" Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and his companions came out of ihram at al-Hudaybiya they sacrificed their sacrificial animals and shaved their heads, and were freed from all the restrictions of ihram without having done tawaf of the House and without their sacrificial animals reaching the Kaba. There is nothing known about the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, ever telling any of his companions, or anybody else that was with him, to make up for anything they had missed or to go back to doing anything they had not finished doing"
"799","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that when Abdullah ibn Umar set out for Makka during the troubles (between al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf and Zubair ibn al-Awwam) he said"
"800","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he had heard that A'isha"
"802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima as- Sakhtayani that a very old man from Basra once said to him"
"803","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"804","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Said ibn Huzaba al-Makhzumi was thrown off his mount while he was in ihram on the road to Makka. He asked after the person in charge of the relay station where he was injured and he found Abdullah ibn Umar"
"805","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakras-Siddiq told Abdullah ibn Umar from A'isha"
"806","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"807","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say that he had heard one of the people of knowledge say that the Hijr was only enclosed so that people would go beyond it as they were making tawaf"
"808","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Jabir ibn Abdullah said"
"809","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to hasten from the Black Stone round to the Black Stone three times and then would walk four circuits normally"
"810","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that when his father did tawaf of the House he would hasten in the first three circuits and say in a low voice"
"811","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that he saw Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr go into ihram for umra at at-Tanim. He said"
"812","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar never used to do tawaf of the House or say between Safa and Marwa if he went into ihram in Makka until he had returned from Mina"
"813","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when the Messenger of Allah"
"814","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that the Messenger of Allah"
"815","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to salute all the corners when he did tawaf of the House and did not omit the Yamani corner unless he was prevented from it"
"816","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to the corner of the Black Stone while he was doing tawaf of the House"
"817","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father would never do two sets of seven tawafs together without praying between them. After every seven tawafs he would pray two rakas"
"818","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf that Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari mentioned to him that he once did tawaf of the House with Umar ibn al-Khattab after subh and when Umar had finished his tawaf he looked and saw that the sun had not yet risen"
"819","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z Zubayr al-Makki said"
"820","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki said"
"821","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"822","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab refused to let one man who had not taken leave of the House pass adh-Dhahran"
"823","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"824","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'l-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Nawfal from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr from Zaynab bint Abi Salama that Umm Salama"
"825","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zubayr al-Makki that Abu Maiz al-Aslami Abdullah ibn Sufyan told him that once"
"826","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that if Sad ibn Abi Waqqas entered Makka late"
"827","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn AIi from his father that Jabir ibn Abdullah said"
"828","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammed ibn AIi from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah"
"829","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar making dua on Safa saying"
"830","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"831","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Sawda bint Abdullah ibn Umar"
"832","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father from Jabir ibn Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah"
"833","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: That A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, used to fast on the Day of Arafah. Al-Qasim said: \And I saw her on the evening of Arafah when the Imam moved on"
"834","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha"
"835","And he narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafah on the days of Mina, going around and saying: \These are only days of eating"
"836","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah"
"837","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"838","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al- Hadi from Abu Murra"
"839","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm that the Messenger of Allah"
"840","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"841","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that he used to see Abdullah ibn Umar sacrificing animals two at a time during hajj and one at a time during umra. He said"
"842","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz once sacrificed a camel during a hajj or an umra"
"843","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Jafar al-Qari that Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia al-Makhzumi sacrificed two camels"
"844","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"845","ahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said, ""If necessary, ride on your sacrificial animal, without burdening it, and if necessary, drink its milk after its young one has drunk its fill, and when you sacrifice it, sacrifice the young one with it"
"846","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that when he brought an animal to be sacrificed from Madina he would garland it and brand it at Dhu'l-Hulayfa"
"847","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"848","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"849","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to drape his sacrificial animals in fine Egyptian linen"
"850","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Abdullah ibn Dinar what Abdullah ibn Umar used to do with the drapings of his animals when the Kaba began to be draped with the kiswa"
"851","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"852","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar never used to tear the drapes of his sacrificial animals"
"853","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to say to his sons"
"854","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the man who was in charge of the sacrificial animal of the Messenger of Allah"
"855","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"856","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili from Abdullah ibn Abbas the same as that"
"857","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"858","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"859","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard the people of knowledge say, ""Someone who dedicates a sacrificial animal for compensation or as part of the hajj should not eat from it."" Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab and AIi ibn Abi Talib and Abu Hurayra were asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife while he was in ihram on hajj. They said, ""The two of them should carry on and complete their hajj. Then they must do hajj again in another year, and sacrifice an animal."" Malik added that AIi ibn Abi Talib said, ""When they then go into ihram for hajj in a future year they should keep apart until they have completed their hajj"
"860","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab asking a group of people"
"861","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that Sulayman ibn Yasar told him that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari once set off to do hajj and then"
"862","Malik related to me from Nafi from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Habbar ibn al-Aswad arrived on the day of sacrifice while Umar ibn al-Khattab was sacrificing his animal and said"
"863","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr al-Makki from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that Abdullah ibn Abbas was asked about a man who had had intercourse with his wife while at Mina before he had done the tawaf al-ifada"
"864","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that lkrama"
"865","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman saying the same about that as what Ikrama related from Ibn Abbas. Malik said"
"866","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Ali ibn Abi Talib used to say"
"867","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to say"
"868","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Urnar used to say"
"869","Yahya related to me from Malik fromAbdullah ibn Abi Bakr that a mawla of Amir bint Abd ar-Rahman called Ruqayya told him that she once set out with Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman to go to Makka. She said"
"870","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sadaqa ibn Yasar al-Makki that a man from the people of Yemen"
"871","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say, ""A woman in ihram should not comb her hair when she leaves ihram until she has cut some of the tresses of her hair, and if she has an animal for sacrifice with her she should not cut off any of her hair until the animal has been killed"
"872","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard one of the people of knowledge say"
"873","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"874","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr used to say"
"875","Malik was asked about whether a man could stand at Arafa"
"876","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"877","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafj from Salim and Ubaydullah"
"878","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Ata ibn Abi Rabah that a mawla of Asma bint Abi Bakr told him"
"879","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Talha ibn Ubaydullah used to send his family and children from Muzdalifa to Mina ahead of him"
"880","Yahya related to.me from Malik that he had heard one of the people of knowledge disapproving of stoning the jamra until after dawn on the day of sacrifice"
"881","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"882","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to spur on his mount in the middle of Muhassir over the distance of a stone's throw"
"883","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said once at Mina, ""This place (where I have just sacrificed), and the whole of Mina, is a place of sacrifice,"" and he said once during umra, ""This place of sacrifice"" meaning Marwa, ""and all the pathways of Makka and its roads are a place of sacrifice"
"884","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman told him that she had heard A'isha"
"885","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Hafsa"
"886","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father from Ali ibn Abi Talib that the Messenger of Allah"
"887","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"888","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to kill his sacrificial animals while they were standing. Malik said"
"889","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"890","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that his father used to go into Makka by night when he was doing umra and do tawaf of the House and say between Safa and Marwa and delay the shaving until the morning"
"891","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that if Abdullah ibn Umar had finished the fast of Ramadan and intended to do hajj"
"892","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to trim his beard and moustache when he shaved at the end of a hajj or umra"
"893","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that a man came to Qasim ibn Muhammad and said"
"894","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar once met a relative of his called al-Mujabbar who had done the tawaf al-ifada but"
"895","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that when Salim ibn Abdullah intended to go into ihram he would call for some scissors and trim his moustache and beard before setting off and before going into ihram"
"896","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"897","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"898","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"899","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Salim ibn Abdullah said"
"900","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to pray dhuhr"
"901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Musa ibn Uqba that Kurayb"
"903","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Adi ibn Thabit al-Ansari that Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi told him that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari told him that he prayed maghrib and isha together at Muzdalifa during the farewell hajj"
"904","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to pray maghrib and isha together at Muzdalifa"
"905","Malik said that the people of Makka who are doing hajj should shorten the prayer to two rakas when at Mina until they go back to Ma ka. Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"906","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab prayed two rakas with everybody when he arrived in Makka. Then"
"907","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab prayed two rakas with the people of Makka"
"908","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knelt down at al-Batḥā' which is in Dhu al-Hulayfah, and prayed there. Nafi' said: \And Abdullah ibn Umar used to do that.\"""""
"909","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"910","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to pray dhuhr"
"911","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said, \No one performing Hajj should spend the nights of Mina behind al-Aqabah.\"""""
"912","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"913","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"914","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to stop at the first two jamras for such a long time that someone standing up would get tired"
"915","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to stop for a long time at the first two jamras saying"
"916","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say \\""Allah is greater\""\"" whenever he threw a pebble while stoning the jamra"""
"917","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard some of the people of knowledge saying"
"918","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Qasim from his father that when people went to stone the jamras they would walk both going there and coming back. The first one to ride was Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan"
"919","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Abd ar-Rahman ibn Qasim"
"920","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"921","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm from his father that Abu'l-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi told him from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"922","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah mentioning that the camel-herders were allowed to throw the stones at night"
"923","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi from his father that the daughter of one of Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd's brothers was bleeding after she had given birth to a child at Muzdalifa. She and Safiyya were delayed and did not arrive at Mina until after the sun had set on the day of sacrifice. Abdullah ibn Umar told them both to stone the jamra at the time they arrived and he did not think that they owed anything. Yahya said that Malik was asked about some one who forgot to stone one of the jamras on one of the days of Mina until it was evening and he said"
"924","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave a khutba to the people at Arafa and taught them the conduct of the hajj"
"925","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"926","Yahya related to me from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim"
"927","[927] He told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha: She said: I came to Mecca and I I am menstruating, and I did not circumambulate the Kaaba, nor between Safa and Marwa, so I complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do what you do. The Hajj must do that, except that you do not circumambulate the House, nor between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, until you have purified yourself.\\nMouta Imam Malik Hadith: 927 Arabic Hadith:"
"928","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha said"
"929","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father from A'isha umm al-muminin that Safiyya bint Huyy began menstruating and so she mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah"
"930","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm from his father from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that A'isha umm al- muminin said to the Messenger of Allah"
"931","Yahya related to me from Malik from AbuRijal Muhammad ibn Abd ar- Rahman from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that when A'isha umm al-muminin was doing hajj with women who were expecting their periods"
"932","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha umm al-muminin that the Messenger of Allah"
"933","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from his father that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman told him that Umm Sulaym bint Milhan asked the Messenger of Allah"
"934","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zubayr that Umar ibn al-Khattab gave the judgement of a ram for a hyena"
"935","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd al-Malik ibn Qurayr from Muhammad ibn Sirin that a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said"
"936","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father used to say"
"937","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"938","Malik said, I still hear that when a person in ihram kills an ostrich, a camel is due."" Malik said, ""I think that for an ostrich egg, one tenth of the price of a camel is due in the same way that there is a newly-born male or female slave for the unborn child of a free woman. The value of the newly-born slave is fifty dinars, and that is one-tenth of what the blood-money for the mother would be. ""Birds from the eagle family, eagles or falcons or vultures count as game for which a price is paid just as a price is paid for any game which a person in ihram kills. For everything for which a penalty is paid, the assessment is the same, whether the animal is old or young. The analogy of that is that the blood-money for the young and the old freeman, are considered to be the same."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said, ""Amir al-muminin, I killed some locusts with my whip when I was in ihram,"" and Umar said to him, ""Give a handful of food"
"939","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and asked him about some locusts he had killed while he was in ihram. Umar said to Kab"
"940","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al- Jazari from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujra that one time he was with the Messenger of Allah"
"941","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd bin Qays from Mujahid Abu'l Hajjaj from Ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujra that the Messenger of Allah"
"942","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ata ibn Abdullah al-Khurasani said that an old man from Suq al-Buram in Kufa had related to him that Kab ibn Ujra said"
"943","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima as- Sakhtayani from Said ibn Jubayr that Abdullah ibn Abbas said"
"944","Malik said, concerning someone who wishes to wear clothes that a person in ihram must not wear, or cut his hair, or touch perfume without necessity, because he finds it easy to pay the compensation, ""No-one must do such things. They are only allowed in cases of necessity, and compensation is owed by whoever does them."" Malik was asked whether the culprit could choose for himself the method of compensation he makes, and he was asked what kind of animal was to be sacrificed, and how much food was to be given, and how many days were to be fasted, and whether the person could delay any of these, or if they had to be done immediately. He answered, 'Whenever there are alternatives in the Book of Allah for the kaffara, the culprit can choose to do whichever of the alternatives he prefers. As for the sacrifice - a sheep, and as for the fasting - three days. As for the food - feeding six poor men, for every poor man two mudds, by the first mudd, the mudd of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."" Malik said, ""I have heard one of the people of knowledge saying, 'When a person in ihram throws something and hits game unintentionally and kills it, he must pay compensation. In the same way, someone outside the Haram who throws anything into the Haram and hits game he did not intend to, killing it, has to pay compensation, because the intentional and the mistaken are in the same position in this matter.' "" Malik said, concerning people who kill game together while they are muhrim or in the Haram, ""I think that each one of them owes a full share. If a sacrificial animal is decided for them, each one of them owes one, and if fasting is decided for them, the full fasting is owed by each one of them. The analogy of that is a group of people who kill a man by mistake and the kaffara for that is that each person among them must free a slave or fast two consecutive months."" Malik said, ""Anyone who stones or hunts game after stoning the jamra and shaving his head but before he has performed the tawaf al-ifada, owes compensation for that game, because Allah the Blessed, the Exalted said, 'And when you leave ihram, then hunt,' and restrictions still remain for someone who has not done the tawaf al-ifada about touching perfume and women."" Malik said, ""The person in ihram does not owe anything for plants he cuts down in the Haram and it has not reached us that anyone has given a decision of anything for it, but O how wrong is what he has done! "" Malik said, concerning some one who was ignorant of, or who forgot the fast of three days in the hajj, or who was ill during them and so did not fast them until he had returned to his community, ""He must offer a sacrificial animal (hady) if he can find one and if not he must fast the three days among his people and the remaining seven after that."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from clsa ibn Talha that Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, stopped for the people at Mina, and they questioned him and a man came and said to him, 'Messenger of Allah, I was unclear about what to do and I shaved before sacrificing,' and the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Sacrifice, and don't worry.' Then another came to him and said 'Messenger of Allah, I was unclear about what to do and I sacrificed before throwing the stones.' He advised, 'Throw, and don't worry.' "" Amr continued, saying that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was not asked about anything done before or after without his saying, ""Do it, and don't worry"
"945","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that when the Messenger of Allah"
"946","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Uqba from Kurayb the mawla of Abdullah ibn Abbas from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah"
"947","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibrahim ibn Abi Abla from Talha ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kariyz that the Messenger of Allah"
"948","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zihad ibn Abi Ziyad the mawla of Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia from Talha ibn Ubaydullah ibn Kariyz that the Messenger of Allah"
"949","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah"
"950","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar was coming from Makka and when he was at Qudayd"
"951","[951] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, in the same way. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 951 Arabic Hadith:"
"952","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala ad-Dili from Muhammad ibn lmran al-Ansari that his father said that Abdullah ibn Umar came upon him while he stopped for a rest under a tall tree on the road to Makka"
"953","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm from Ibn Abi Mulayka that Umar ibn al-Khattab passed a leprous woman doing tawaf of the House"
"954","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to say that the area between the corner of the Black Stone and the door of the Kaba was called al-Multazam"
"955","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban mentioning that a certain man passed Abu Dharr at ar-Rabadha (which was about 30 miles from Madina) and Abu Dharr asked him"
"956","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab about making a condition in the hajj that one could leave ihram at any place where an obstacle befell one and he said"
"957","Malik said, concerning a woman who had never been on hajj, ""If she doesn't have a mahram, or if she has, but he cannot come with her, she does not abandon Allah's making of the hajj obligatory for her. Let her go in a group of women."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that A'isha umm al-muminin used to say, ""Someone performing hajj at-tamattu who does not have a sacrificial animal fasts (three days) from the time he enters ihram for the hajj till the Day of Arafa, and if he does not fast then, he fasts the days of Mina."" Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn Abdullah that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say the same concerning that, as the words of A'isha, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with her"
